Z||000000||Jason Kamrud||05-15-2001||10:57 PM||||What kind of decklid scoops are people using these days?  Has anyone ever tried using a shaker hood scoop & air cleaner setup from the older (1970's) trans am's? I am doing my first SBC conversion, and I was thinking that this would look pretty mean with the open end facing back. The carb would have to be centered left-right to the decklid, and you would have to use a flat decklid, but otherwise I bet it would work great & look mean.  Scrapyards sell the scoop & air cleaner setup for like $40-50, wich is what you pay for one of them cheezy-lookin Taiwan scoops.<P>Please let me know if anyone has tried this...I would really like to know what it looks like, and I want to be able to show off my 'poncho power' (I just won't tell 'em it's a chevy engine!)<P>------------------<BR>Jason Kamrud||||reg||6
